Jazz emerged in the late 19th and early 20th centuries in New Orleans, Louisiana. It was a fusion of various musical styles, including African American spirituals, ragtime, and European marching band music. The African American community in New Orleans was a melting pot of cultures, with influences from the Caribbean and West African rhythms, which played a significant role in shaping the unique sound of jazz.

