//
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The 1920s and 1930s were the golden age of swing music. This period saw the rise of big bands, such as Duke Ellington and Count Basie, and the development of swing dance styles like the Lindy hop. The music became a symbol of the Roaring Twenties and the cultural shift during the Great Depression.

