//
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The 1940s and 1950s were marked by the emergence of bebop and cool jazz. Musicians like Charlie Parker and Dizzy Gillespie revolutionized the genre with their complex chord progressions and fast tempos. Cool jazz, on the other hand, was characterized by a more laid-back and introspective style, with artists like Miles Davis and John Coltrane at the forefront.

